1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,564
Welcome to the Downhole Studio training video from QuakeLogic.

2
00:00:04,564 --> 00:00:16,519
In the next few minutes you will take a downhole seismic survey from raw SEG-2 records to reviewed P and S picks, a layered velocity model, Vs30, and a finished report.

3
00:00:20,419 --> 00:00:27,468
The first time Downhole Studio starts, it offers a 14-day free trial, or activation with a license key.

4
00:00:27,468 --> 00:00:30,891
Licensing sends only a hashed computer identifier.

5
00:00:30,891 --> 00:00:33,902
Your survey data never leaves your computer.

6
00:00:33,902 --> 00:00:37,724
When the trial is running, the start screen opens.

7
00:00:40,824 --> 00:00:41,987
Click New Project.

8
00:00:41,987 --> 00:00:44,571
Give the survey a name and a job number.

9
00:00:44,571 --> 00:00:54,273
Everything you do from here on is kept in one project file, together with the original records, so another engineer can reproduce your analysis.

10
00:00:54,973 --> 00:00:59,206
On the Import page, drag in the SEG-2 files, or add a whole folder.

11
00:00:59,206 --> 00:01:02,491
Every file is inspected before anything is imported.

12
00:01:02,491 --> 00:01:09,567
The checks list sample rates, channels, duplicates, and the depth sequence, as errors, warnings, or information.

13
00:01:09,567 --> 00:01:11,399
Nothing is repaired silently.

14
00:01:11,399 --> 00:01:14,115
When the preview looks right, click Import.

15
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:18,306
The original files are stored byte-for-byte, with checksums.

16
00:01:21,406 --> 00:01:27,748
On the Geometry page, enter the borehole details and the horizontal offsets of the P and S sources.

17
00:01:27,748 --> 00:01:33,194
The two sources have their own offsets, and the borehole diagram updates as you type.

18
00:01:33,194 --> 00:01:43,139
Then assign each record to a depth and a shot type, here by acquisition order: one P shot and two opposite S shots at every depth, from the top down.

19
00:01:46,239 --> 00:01:48,832
Before processing, look at every trace.

20
00:01:48,832 --> 00:01:52,488
The waveform viewer shows all depths, raw or processed.

21
00:01:52,488 --> 00:01:57,673
Scroll to zoom in time, and click a trace to see its details in the inspector.

22
00:01:57,673 --> 00:02:02,727
The spectrum below shows the dominant frequency of the selected trace.

23
00:02:05,827 --> 00:02:08,613
Processing never changes the recorded data.

24
00:02:08,613 --> 00:02:16,195
Each component has its own chain of steps, applied to a copy, and every step can be switched off, edited, or removed.

25
00:02:16,195 --> 00:02:18,463
For picking, keep processing light.

26
00:02:18,463 --> 00:02:25,602
Here a gentle band-pass is added to the horizontal components, to make the shear waves easier to review.

27
00:02:26,302 --> 00:02:31,283
A reference geophone at the source records the true moment of every hammer blow.

28
00:02:31,283 --> 00:02:34,769
Pick its onsets automatically, then choose a correction.

29
00:02:34,769 --> 00:02:43,921
Subtract reference onset measures every arrival from the moment the source was struck, which removes the trigger delay and the shot-to-shot jitter.

30
00:02:43,921 --> 00:02:46,189
The raw times are always kept.

31
00:02:49,289 --> 00:02:52,400
On the P Picks page, run the automatic picker.

32
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:54,429
The AIC picker is recommended.

33
00:02:54,429 --> 00:03:07,545
Every automatic pick gets a confidence score, and the inspector explains it: signal-to-noise ratio, onset sharpness, agreement between algorithms, and consistency with neighbouring depths.

34
00:03:08,245 --> 00:03:09,392
Review every depth.

35
00:03:09,392 --> 00:03:14,524
Click to place a pick, drag it, or nudge it one sample at a time with the arrow keys.

36
00:03:14,524 --> 00:03:18,146
When you agree with the automatic picks, mark them reviewed.

37
00:03:18,146 --> 00:03:22,350
Manual picks are never overwritten by running the picker again.

38
00:03:25,450 --> 00:03:28,485
Shear waves are picked on the horizontal components.

39
00:03:28,485 --> 00:03:36,247
Because the S source is struck at both ends, the shear wave reverses polarity between the two shots, while P energy and noise do not.

40
00:03:36,247 --> 00:03:44,183
Downhole Studio picks on the half difference of the two shots, and the depth detail overlays them, so you can confirm the shear arrival.

41
00:03:44,183 --> 00:03:52,462
If the probe rotated between depths, polarization analysis finds the best horizontal direction, but it is only applied when you choose.

42
00:03:55,562 --> 00:03:59,424
The travel-time graph shows the corrected arrivals against depth.

43
00:03:59,424 --> 00:04:03,228
Each straight segment is a layer, and its slope is 1 / velocity.

44
00:04:03,228 --> 00:04:08,219
Click Suggest boundaries, review the suggestions, and apply the ones you agree with.

45
00:04:08,219 --> 00:04:11,903
You can drag any boundary, and everything updates immediately.

46
00:04:11,903 --> 00:04:21,811
Choose the method: layer regression, interval velocities, or refracted-ray layer stripping, which follows Snell's law and is the most accurate near the surface.

47
00:04:24,911 --> 00:04:31,868
The Engineering page computes Poisson's ratio and the shear, Young's, and bulk moduli for every layer.

48
00:04:31,868 --> 00:04:33,573
Density is never assumed.

49
00:04:33,573 --> 00:04:41,690
Enter measured values, one constant, or deliberately choose an empirical estimate, which is then labelled as estimated.

50
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:47,956
Vs30 is calculated from measured data only, unless you explicitly allow extrapolation.

51
00:04:51,056 --> 00:04:54,621
The Results page shows how trustworthy the analysis is.

52
00:04:54,621 --> 00:05:02,334
Every automatic check is explained in plain language, and clicking a finding takes you to the depth or layer concerned.

53
00:05:02,334 --> 00:05:03,890
The verdict is advisory.

54
00:05:03,890 --> 00:05:10,383
It does not certify compliance with any standard, and results always need professional review.

55
00:05:13,483 --> 00:05:22,545
Finally, fill in the client, site, and company details on the Report page, choose the sections, and preview the report page by page.

56
00:05:22,545 --> 00:05:31,401
Generate PDF writes the finished report, with the methodology, quality control, figures, tables, and the full processing history.

57
00:05:31,401 --> 00:05:38,323
Tables export to Excel and CSV at full precision, and every figure exports as PNG, SVG, or PDF.

58
00:05:39,023 --> 00:05:40,973
That is the complete workflow.

59
00:05:40,973 --> 00:05:48,188
The sample project on the start screen shows a finished survey, and the field guide explains how to record one.

60
00:05:48,188 --> 00:05:52,163
Thank you for choosing Downhole Studio from QuakeLogic.

